#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138073 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138536 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6090342d-3d4e-519f-ab7d-3fb6df6e92a8" :knowledge-point/title "Representing \"Or\" Inequalities on Number Lines"}] :question/id #uuid "014723fc-0b7d-5212-a41e-73847f5adb00" :question/math-academy-id "e-13011" :question/problem "Represent the inequality $x < -2$ or $x \\geq  1$ on a number line." :question/worked-solution "The inequality $x < -2$ or $x \\geq  1$ means that $x$ can take any value less than $-2,$ or greater than or equal to $1.$\n\nTo represent this on a number line, we graph the two separate inequalities:\n\n- the inequality $x < -2$ consists of an open circle at $-2$ and an arrow to the left.\n\n- the inequality $x \\geq 1$ consists of a closed circle at $1$ and an arrow to the right.\n\nThe resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/a1/a1067762a65fca32ca847a58dd47b07258f4ce58df20e45435df8a0a9e5d6f90.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138538 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9106723c-b8b0-586e-8c2b-9bb4f50bc945" :knowledge-point/title "Representing \"And\" Inequalities on Number Lines"}] :question/id #uuid "21eace75-0b5a-5b37-903c-c238e3821bee" :question/math-academy-id "e-13012" :question/problem "![](images/b4/b4906893158bb5dc9f55363dcf2edc2ae1d30d8acff7121041d4a849ee73cbce.png)\n\nWhat inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?" :question/worked-solution "The red segment contains all values between  $-2$ and $0.$ In addition,\n\n- the closed circle at $-2$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-2,$ while\n\n- the open circle at $0$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $0.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $-2 \\leq  x <    0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138075 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138537 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32daa2fb-e5fa-5e44-b6f2-5d815d9145af" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying \"Or\" Inequalities Given on Number Lines"}] :question/id #uuid "e5b6a9dc-3a19-5496-9e22-d953ff4eb647" :question/math-academy-id "e-13018" :question/problem "![](images/7a/7ae1311495d3fcb290bdf3f4b303224415e2e55c5ae1af8a82efd1f3aa2572b4.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?" :question/worked-solution "The red rays contain all values less than $-4$ or greater than $-1.$ In addition, \n\n- the open circle at $-4$ implies that $x$ cannot be equal to $-4,$ and\n\n- the closed circle at $-1$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-1.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents $x <    -4$ or $x \\geq -1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138076 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138539 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a707a741-0208-5a74-8478-ac05ff2673ab" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying \"And\" Inequalities Given on Number Lines"}] :question/id #uuid "347520ff-e759-5d99-acf7-0bc8a8f26689" :question/math-academy-id "e-13019" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f7a8d632deb19af6f7efc30182fb349f766c3ca7c10ba6567f9e2fd2e02e4b07.png)\n\nWhich inequality corresponds to the highlighted region shown on the number line above?" :question/worked-solution "The red segment contains all values between  $-2$ and $\\dfrac{3}{2}.$ In addition,\n\n- the closed circle at $-2$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $-2,$ while\n\n- the closed circle at $\\dfrac32$ implies that $x$ can be equal to $\\dfrac32.$\n\nTherefore, the highlighted region represents  $-2 \\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue} \\leq }  x \\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue} \\leq }  \\dfrac32 .$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447252 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186138537 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32daa2fb-e5fa-5e44-b6f2-5d815d9145af" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying \"Or\" Inequalities Given on Number Lines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "113fb996-f646-5f2c-a2c1-2ddf035922b9